<!--Post: 8302--><!--Time: 1109043371-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8302"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 7:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Many of the folks who have grown up around trains become train collectors and belong to model railroaders clubs.   <BR> <BR>I was just wondering if there is a club in the Wichita area. Or a train museum.  BTK may belong to such a group or visit a museum to talk about trains if he is fond of them. <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8302-->
<!--Post: 8380--><!--Time: 1109099321-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8380"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 11:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m beginning to think that everything he said in the bio is designed to throw us off. The bit about trains is very vague. We don&#39;t even know for sure if he did grow up in the area, or where his mom may have dated the railroad cop. Many people have an interest in railroading but confine it to looking at a train going by, or occasionally visiting a museum, but never getting involved. If someone using the &#34;railroad&#34; angle comes up with something, they will be very lucky.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8380-->
<!--Post: 8435--><!--Time: 1109127245-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8435"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 6:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tadpole, <BR> <BR>I looked up model trains in the 2002 Wichita directory and came up with Engine House Hobbies. Their web site is rrtrains.com<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8435-->
<!--Post: 8436--><!--Time: 1109127302-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8436"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 6:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->agreed. a lot of the stuff &#40;if not all&#41; on the btk bio is crap. it&#39;s designed to throw everybody off.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8436-->
<!--Post: 8439--><!--Time: 1109128845-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 7:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kmuw.org/programming/wrrs/bios/pearce.html" target=_top>http://www.kmuw.org/programming/wrrs/bios/pearce.h tml</a> <BR> <BR>I put this under general discussion as a string, but it belongs here...sorry<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8439-->
<!--Post: 8453--><!--Time: 1109137141-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8453"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 9:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This person looks way too social and successful to be a POI, in my opinion. But the fact that he matches some of the BTK &#34;fake clues&#34; makes me wonder if he was used in their construction - possibly because BTK has a grudge against him, or a dislike for him.  As a public person, I&#39;m sure BTK knows who he is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8453-->
<!--Post: 8454--><!--Time: 1109137531-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8454"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is a toy train club in wichita. google that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8454-->
<!--Post: 8475--><!--Time: 1109169987-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8475"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 6:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The important thing is right now, we don&#39;t know what is &#34;crap&#34; and what isn&#39;t. We do know he is clever and controlling, apparently smart enough to keep all his secrets for all these years. I just can&#39;t imagine him not saying something incriminating at one time or another. But even if he did, maybe jokingly, he wasn&#39;t taken seriously  maybe because of his social status.  <BR> <BR>I suggested a Railroader Club simply because having grown up around trains the other half and I  collect trains, have a layout in the basement, belong to a club. Nostalgia.  <BR> <BR>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8475-->
<!--Post: 8655--><!--Time: 1109269924-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:newmilleniumwriter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 10:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tadpole - there is a club.  At least one in the general area.  A few years ago they had a major set up at a mall in Hutchinson, KS.  I don&#39;t remember if anyone said how many members there were - but the display was gigantic!  I was astounded and I didn&#39;t even take a good look at it.  I remember one guy, who is now in his 30s who was big in that group.  Maybe I&#39;ll give him a holler - if he is still in the area.  <BR> <BR>You never know - it doesn&#39;t hurt to put out theories.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8655-->
<!--Post: 8692--><!--Time: 1109289210-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8692"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 3:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve followed this case for quite some time and I&#39;m glad someone brought this up.  My 5-year-old son loves trains so I take him to all of the model train shows here in K.C.   <BR> <BR>Over the holidays there were several displays at Union Station and recently the Great American Train Show &#40;I think that was the name???&#41; was down next to Kemper Arena.  With all of the overgrown children in attendance, like me, I couldn&#39;t help but think that it&#39;s possible that he either attends these shows or maybe even has his own display.  I wonder if LE has been smart enough to at least consider this? <BR> <BR>Then again, maybe his interest in trains is complete b.s.  We know he loves to deceive.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8692-->
<!--Post: 8697--><!--Time: 1109291238-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8697"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I should have mentioned that the link I posted, above, was part of three three unsolicited emails that I receieved on my private account &#40;which refered to this board&#41;. I only looked at it briefly then passed it to this thread as a source of information. <BR> <BR>It is not mean&#39;t to point to anyone associated with the site as suspect, but rather as a source of information to follow up info on &#34;a&#34; suspect. <BR> <BR>I didn&#39;t think much about it because the info in the bio stating BTK&#39;s interest in trains has been paraphrased by the police and the original &#34;clues&#34; may have been inadvertently altered in the process.  <BR> <BR>Personally I feel the &#34;train&#34; reference is weak as a clue, but I don&#39;t want people who are working it to be denied any possible source just because I&#39;m not seeing something that they can.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8697-->
</table></td></tr></table>
